--- stdout ---
Add the new network and moderation sources to the build

Wire the resync, A7 journal and F6 panel sources into MSBuild and Meson.

Compare snapshots by the controlled actor's inventory role

The comparator was selecting Activity1's brain; use the controlled actor so the retained pair matches.

Record A7 recovery events on session, tickets and ownership

Session heartbeats, loaded-ticket hashes and local unit ownership feed the existing A7 journal.

Initialize saved-game modules and use the lobby shared clock

Selected modules get writable save storage, and lobby waits use the session clock plus transfer progress instead of a flat timeout.

Restore peer-local player, UI and aliases after a restore

Capture and reload local bindings, camera, input and GUI-owned graphs without copying the host presentation onto a returning peer.

Give the host a live F6 panel and codec-17 seat snapshots

Replace stop-message notices with authenticated seat snapshots, keep seat metadata, and show a persistent roster.

Add A7 journal helpers for recovery-arm traces

Emit bounded JSON events the Mac A7 driver already reads.

Keep ACraft exit selection and AHuman inventory across checkpoint load

Checkpoint construction applies the persisted exit and skips empty-hand startup equip.

Skip registry mutation when privately adopting a persisted UniqueID

A non-registering faithful clone takes the saved id without unregistering the canonical object.

Restore typed native aliases and isolate craft-fixture clones

Borrowed owners keep their Lua class, and craft-fixture clones leave the source graph registered.

Restore complete input, drop-map ownership and exact-target priming

Replay acknowledged commands and delayed inputs after a heal, keep the drop map, and prime the resync at the exact saved target.

Bound a resync envelope around archive, acks and pending commands

Encode ownership maps, acknowledged command sequences and pending inputs in a size-capped envelope. Raise the lobby state-chunk ceiling so a complete-input archive fits.

Carry player-binding observations on the command wire

A peer's local slots travel as codec-18 PlayerBindings with a sender-local sequence so a pending command can cross a resync.


